      "side": 1,
      "message": "What are we gaining from having these two functions? It seems like in the implementations of vSkLog when comparing it to SkDebugf they are just replacing a va_start call with a va_copy call. Is it really cleaner to have the extra indirection to do the va_start in one place, but still need to add the extra copy call in vSkLog?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 20,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 20,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "114f4f0483f9214043628ebb351a451894d3fc69",
