        "id": 11964
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-03T18:36:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "2 functions let us share an implementation while having 2 entry points (legacy SkDebugf and SkLog) while we migrate.\nThe reason why we don\u0027t just have SkDebug forwarding to SkLog is because we accept variable arguments in both SkDebugf and SkLog. The vSkLog function (soon to be called SkLogVAList) assumes that SkDebugf and SkLog have already converted the variable arguments into a va_list with va_start. The va_copy was already there and was needed because we are printing to 2 places that would consume the va_list.",
      "parentUuid": "93152dde_f94b353a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 20,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 20,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "114f4f0483f9214043628ebb351a451894d3fc69",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
